  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AUC/JFA L&#xf6;nefond 2013-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AUC/JFA Salaries 2013-2017 - AUC/JFA Salaries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program st&#xf6;d till AUs program f&#xf6;r fred och s&#xe4;kerhet. Inlcuderar bland annat medling, SSR, SALW, l&#xf6;ner och st&#xf6;d till f&#xe4;ltkontor i            konfliktomr&#xe5;den.                                                       JFA-support to AU Peace and Security Architecture APSA.The 2 phase   includes support to the PSD and covers 85% of the staffs salaries.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Program support to AU peace and security program. Includes mediation, SSR, SALW, salaries, liaison offices and more                                                                                                JFA-st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r utveckling av AUs freds- och s&#xe4;kerhetsarkitektur APSA.  Denna andra fas avser st&#xf6;d till 85% av avdelningens  anst&#xe4;lldas       l&#xf6;ner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the The Joint Financing Arrangement for Support to the Employment of AUC Personnel Working in the Peace and Security Programme (also referred to as the&#xa0;JFA Salaries or &quot;Salary Fund&quot;) was to strengthen the capacity of the African Union in the field of peace and security, by supporting staff costs to enable the Peace and Security Department of the AU to hire necessary technical staff. It follows on from a phase one, 2010-2012.&#xa0;
Contributing partners have varied over time, and at the outset of the JFA 2013-2017, included European Union (thoughout), Germany, Sweden, Norway, Denmark, Netherlands and the UK.&#xa0;
The activity period for this contribution was from 2013-06-12 to 2017-12-31, with a total of agreed and disbursed funds, amounting to SEK 54&#xa0;250&#xa0;000. The activity period was aligned with the AU Strategic Plan 2013-2017. At the end of 2017, the AU requested an extension of this JFA for an additional year. Following recommendations by Swedish National Auditors Office after contribution review in November 2017, this extension was however assessed in a new contribution (UM2018/03914).</narrative>
  </description>
